# CAD/KCL generated files
cad/*.stl
cad/*.png
cad/*.jpg
cad/*.txt
cad/output.*
# DIMENSIONS.md is an on-demand render of cad/config/dimensions.yaml (the source
# of truth) — never committed; a versioned copy kept drifting. Render locally
# with `python cad/scripts/gen_dimensions.py` if you want the readable view.
cad/DIMENSIONS.md
cad/project.toml
cad/**/project.toml
cad/**/thumbnail.png

# Generated CAD artifacts — the build scripts are the source of truth, so
# nothing under cad/out/ is versioned as a living document. The whole tree is
# build output: parts/assemblies/drawings, neutral exports (STEP/STL/glTF),
# renders, the doit hash database, gate stamps, per-task logs, inspection
# snapshots and staged release bundles. Rebuild with `doit` (dodo.py); snapshot
# binaries only at tagged releases (see README). Ignored WHOLESALE rather than
# per-subdirectory so a new output kind can never leak into the tree untracked.
cad/out/

# Downloaded release bundles (gh release download); large binaries, never
# committed — the release on GitHub is the snapshot.
download/

# Local scratch exports and review conversions.
tmp/

# Comparison gallery — DERIVED, regenerable artefacts (they drift as the model or
# the reference crops change, so tracking them dirtied the tree on every rebuild
# and shipped a stale showcase). Refreshed offline (cad/comparisons/tools/
# render_offline.py -> Blender + gallery.py) and published INSIDE each release
# bundle (cut_release.py: refresh_comparisons). Only manifest.json (pose/align
# source of truth) + ATTRIBUTION.md / README.md / tools stay tracked; the reference
# CROPS regenerate from the pinned `references` submodule via prepare_reference,
# so the release refresh rewrites nothing tracked (never dirties the tagged tree).
cad/comparisons/ref/
cad/comparisons/render/
cad/comparisons/composite/
cad/comparisons/scores.json
cad/comparisons/index.html
# Per-iteration part-fit deltas (pose_studio.py Export Part Deltas -> map_deltas.py);
# scratch tied to one geometry snapshot, consumed into a build-script edit then discarded.
cad/comparisons/findings/

# Mesa OSMesa software-GL DLL fetched on demand for headless VTK rendering
# (cad/comparisons/tools/osmesa_win.py; ~55 MB, regenerable from pal1000/mesa-dist-win)
cad/comparisons/tools/.osmesa-cache/

# Parity-test scratch (cad/comparisons/tools/parity_check.py)
cad/comparisons/.parity_sw/

# Pose-presentation benchmark outputs (cad/docs/pose-presentation-benchmark.md):
# renders, stimuli, sandboxes, results are regenerable. The bench CODE and the
# ground-truth cases.jsonl (under cad/comparisons/bench/, NOT out/) stay tracked.
cad/comparisons/bench/out/

# SolidworksMCP runtime state (agent memory, checkpoint scripts, RAG cache) and
# the generated API docs index — machine-local, regenerated by the MCP server
.solidworks_mcp/
.generated/docs-index/

# verify.py / shell run logs (covers the old .logs/.render-venv/ too)
.logs/
.render-mesa*
.render-osmesa/
.render_diff_v020/
.7zr.exe
.mesalib.conda
.gl_test.png
.cf_repo.json

# Per-machine build-cache role (off|ro|rw) read by cad/scripts/_artifact_cache.py
.harmonic-remote-cache-mode

# playwright-cli skill scratch (machine-local browser session state)
.playwright-cli/

# machine-local dev-tooling binaries (Jaeger + native Aspire dashboard + dotnet
# runtime for local OTel trace/log viewing — see memory/otel-trace-local-viewing.md)
.tools/

# Agent worktrees (transient, per-session; never an artefact of the repo)
.claude/worktrees/

# meshprobe inspection-session state (local tool cache, never versioned)
.meshprobe/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing areas (book / web / kickstarter / logbook / ai-story)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Quarto book: rendered output, its cache, and the figures copied out of
# cad/out by book/scripts/collect_figures.py. The CAD renders are build
# artefacts (see cad/out/ above) — the book references them by a stable path,
# it does not version them. figures/hand/ IS tracked.
book/_book/
book/.quarto/
book/figures/generated/
book/*.pdf
book/*.epub

# Vite/three.js simulator: dependencies, build output, and the GLB it loads
# (exported by `doit export` into cad/out/gltf/, copied to web/public/).
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
web/public/models/

# Campaign binaries: renders, video cuts and page exports are regenerated from
# the model or uploaded to Kickstarter — the inventory in
# kickstarter/assets/README.md is what's tracked, not the assets themselves.
kickstarter/assets/**/*.png
kickstarter/assets/**/*.jpg
kickstarter/assets/**/*.jpeg
kickstarter/assets/**/*.mp4
kickstarter/assets/**/*.mov

# Logbook photographs are large and often personal; keep the write-ups tracked
# and store the raw media outside the repo (link it from the entry).
logbook/media/

# Local agent-session transcripts kept as a backup. Its own git repo, so a bare
# `git add -A` picks it up as a gitlink; it is machine-local and may contain
# paths and personal detail, so it never belongs in this repo.
agent-sessions-backup/
